  "title": "Where each Res(xor) route to the sphere's count stops",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "No route of the frozen transfer statement carries a regular, depth-restricted or dag-like Res(xor) size bound to the sphere's count NAE(K_k). (Lemma 1) Braun's generic criterion (Theorem 9.1 of arXiv 2609.23015) applied to any polynomial system with an F2 polynomial-calculus refutation of degree d <= 2v/3 over v variables certifies at most exp(d^2/(6v)) nodes; the count has degree at most its resolution width plus 1, O(sqrt n), so the criterion certifies only a constant (R2). (Lemma 2) The bit-PHP sources would need a reduction from PIGEON to the count with each point a single parity; reductions by ordinary decision trees of polylogarithmic depth do not exist (PPP^dt is not contained in PPADS^dt, Beame et al. 1998), and none by parities is known (R1). (Lemma 3) No 1-stifling gadget is affine, so the published lifted sources enter the count only through non-affine points (R3). (Lemma 4) The count and its xor-lift reduce to each other by affine maps, so the xor-lift is no new source (R4).",
